{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/13/codegen_prompts/3.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/13`\n- 题号：`3`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/13/3.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"3\">\n- `description`：在一组彩色条中，根据条的高度排名确定其在输出中的水平位置，并用高度值对应的图例颜色重绘。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格上方有一行颜色图例：从左到右排列 5 个不同颜色的像素（如 Red、Orange、Yellow、Green、Blue），分别对应排名 1（最矮）到 5（最高）。\n  - 网格下方有 5 个底部对齐的一像素宽垂直彩色条，高度各不相同（1-5 像素不等），全部使用 Grey 颜色。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 按高度从矮到高对 5 个条排名（最矮为排名 1）。\n  - 将每个条按排名重新排列到输出中的对应列位置（排名 1 在最左列，排名 5 在最右列）。\n  - 每个条用图例中对应排名的颜色重绘。\n  - 保持底部对齐。图例保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：条的高度同时决定了两件事：输出中的列位置（排名决定位置）和颜色（排名索引图例）——解题者需要从样例中同时归纳位置重排和颜色映射两层规则。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/37ce87bb, train/b7955b3c, train/ad38a9d0, train/9b30e358, train/2e65ae53, train/20fb2937, train/b25e450b, train/34cfa167\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"37ce87bb\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2845\nmechanism=0.3220\nlexical=0.0273\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, output:same_size, relation:aligned, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/37ce87bb.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/37ce87bb.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nCompute a grey result bar by adding teal bar heights and subtracting red bar heights.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has a dominant background and several bottom-aligned one-cell-wide vertical bars.\n- Teal bars are positive operands; red bars are negative operands.\n- The penultimate column is an empty result slot.\n\nRule\n- Keep every input bar unchanged.\n- Compute result height = total teal bar height - total red bar height.\n- Paint that many bottom cells of the penultimate column grey.\n\nKey insight\n- The bars encode arithmetic by height, with color providing the sign.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"bottom-aligned one-cell-wide teal and red vertical bars\",\n  \"dst\": \"empty penultimate column result slot\",\n  \"transform\": \"paint a bottom-aligned grey result bar whose height is total teal bar height minus total red bar height\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"b7955b3c\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2665\nmechanism=0.3426\nlexical=0.0174\ncode_feature=0.2500\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, object:template, output:same_size, relation:aligned, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/b7955b3c.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/b7955b3c.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nReplace gray plus-shaped damage masks with the hidden colors of the rectilinear mosaic.\n\nInput structure:\n- Color 8 appears only as isolated 3x3 plus masks.\n- The non-mask pixels are visible parts of a clean grid made from horizontal\n  and vertical color regions.\n\nRule:\n- Treat every color-8 pixel as unknown damage and leave all other pixels fixed.\n- First copy unknown pixels from exact matching parallel rows or columns.\n- Then fill any remaining mask cells from opposite-side continuations and the\n  better-supported local straight edge.\n\nKey insight:\n- The gray pluses are occluders, not objects; the underlying colors are\n  determined by repeated line templates and nearby axis-aligned boundaries.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"color-8 3x3 plus masks over a rectilinear color mosaic\",\n  \"transform\": \"treat color-8 pixels as hidden cells; restore each mask from matching parallel rows or columns and local straight-edge continuation, leaving all visible pixels unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"ad38a9d0\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2725\nmechanism=0.3027\nlexical=0.0332\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:template, output:same_size, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/ad38a9d0.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/ad38a9d0.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRecolor each placeholder object according to its normalized shape while leaving the background fixed.\n\nInput structure\nA same-size grid with one dominant background color and one foreground\nplaceholder color forming separated 4-connected objects.\n\nRule\nReplace every placeholder object by the color assigned to its exact\ntranslation-normalized mask; all background pixels remain unchanged.\n\nKey insight\nThe input objects are a shape legend with repeated instances: identical\nmasks always receive identical colors, independent of their position.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"4-connected placeholder-color foreground objects on a dominant background\",\n  \"transform\": \"recolor each object by exact translation-normalized mask: right-elbow triomino -> yellow, stair tetromino -> teal, plus pentomino -> green, 3-vertical bar -> red, 2-vertical bar -> maroon, 2x3 rectangle -> grey; leave background unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"9b30e358\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2420\nmechanism=0.3062\nlexical=0.0188\ncode_feature=0.2500\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, output:same_size, relation:aligned, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/9b30e358.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/9b30e358.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRepeat the bottom foreground motif upward until it fills the whole grid.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- The only foreground pixels occupy a contiguous block of rows at the bottom.\n- That bottom block is the complete vertical motif, including its background cells.\n\nRule\n- Copy the bottom motif rows repeatedly upward across the full grid.\n- Preserve horizontal alignment and vertical phase: the original first motif row remains at its input row.\n- The output shape is unchanged.\n\nKey insight\nThe blank rows above the bottom foreground block are missing repetitions of the same row motif, not empty space.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"bottom contiguous row motif containing all foreground pixels plus its background cells\",\n  \"transform\": \"repeat the motif rows upward with the same vertical phase until every row is filled\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"2e65ae53\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2278\nmechanism=0.2591\nlexical=0.0179\ncode_feature=0.4000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, output:same_size, relation:aligned, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/2e65ae53.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/2e65ae53.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill every lattice slot from the color assigned to that slot position by the other lattices.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- The largest foreground color forms several one-pixel-thick rectangular lattice frames.\n- The frame lines divide each lattice into the same row-by-column set of rectangular slots; some slots already contain one non-frame color.\n\nRule:\n- Infer a color for each logical slot position from the colored slots across all lattice frames.\n- Repaint every slot interior in every lattice with the inferred color for its row/column position.\n- Keep the frame lines and all background outside frames unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- Slot sizes vary by frame, but the complete color pattern is indexed by lattice slot position rather than by absolute pixel size or location.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"colored slot s in any lattice frame\",\n  \"dst\": \"slot interior d in any lattice frame\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.logical_slot_position == d.logical_slot_position\",\n  \"transform\": \"fill d with s.color, preserving frame lines and outside background\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"20fb2937\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2345\nmechanism=0.2690\nlexical=0.0181\ncode_feature=0.4000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:template, relation:aligned, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/20fb2937.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/20fb2937.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nReplace each marker below the separator with the mapped top legend square centered on that marker.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background surrounds a top legend, one solid non-background separator row, and a lower marker field.\n- The legend contains equal-size filled square sprites, with a singleton marker below each sprite and aligned to its center column.\n- The lower field contains only background and marker colors from the legend.\n\nRule:\n- Pair legend markers to legend sprites by left-to-right position.\n- Discard the legend and separator; keep the grid width and the rows below the separator.\n- In the lower field, replace every marker pixel by a filled square of the paired sprite color, centered at the marker location.\n\nKey insight: The top area is a positional color legend, and the actual output is the post-separator marker field expanded by that legend.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"filled square sprite s in the top legend\",\n  \"dst\": \"lower marker d as center anchor\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d.color == singleton marker color below s\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"top legend maps each singleton marker color to its filled square sprite\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"rows below the separator, same width\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
